{"id":"10f8c2e1-37c7-4439-afac-a45a03c602ba","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2eaf38cbff6ebeaa","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/history/runs-say.ts","baseline":{"blob":"888cc68696569bb457148f29ba0a87a3e2bff137","start":0,"end":65},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Feature","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/util/silo/features","\""]},"context":{"after":"4b4004063c813150"}},"payload":{"text":"What runs say of a feature (pure): whether its code ran. A feature's own code is where it's registered (its inline handler)\nand the declarations its registration names; what ran is each run's statements, by file, in the text it ran.\n\nexercised   a statement in its own code ran;\ndormant     its file ran, but its own code never did;\nunobserved  no run ran its file: nothing to say yet.\n\nWhat it reaches beyond its own code doesn't count (a helper many features share would make them all look exercised), nor\ndoes the statement that registers it, which runs whether or not it's ever used: only code strictly inside counts.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:53.211Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:53.211Z"}
